module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SymGenDegreeOne.ProjectiveBundleTwists

/-!
# The tautological map of a projective bundle onto its degree-one twist

Tag 01NR's twist datum of a graded algebra `𝒜` on `S` carries, in every nonnegative degree `n`,
a map `ψ n : 𝒜_n ⟶ π_*𝒪(n)` on the base. Its transpose under the adjunction
`π^* ⊣ π_*` is a map `π^*𝒜_n ⟶ 𝒪(n)` on the relative `Proj`. At `n = 1` and `𝒜 = Sym(ℰ)`,
precomposed with the canonical `ℰ ⟶ Sym¹(ℰ)`, this is the tautological map

  `π^*ℰ ⟶ 𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(1)`

that `Stacks.Divisors.BundleSplittingDatum.quot` asks for. This file writes it down for the
canonical twist datum `Stacks.SymGraded.projectiveBundleTwistData`, so that `quot` is a
construction rather than an argument.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting.tautologicalTwistMap`: the transpose of `ψ n` at the
  canonical twist datum of `Sym(ℰ)`, a map `π^*Sym^n(ℰ) ⟶ 𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(n)`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting.tautologicalTwist`: the degree-one twist `𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(1)` as a
  module on the bundle.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting.tautologicalMap`: the tautological map
  `π^*ℰ ⟶ 𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(1)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting.isInvertible_tautologicalTwist`: the target `𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(1)` is
  invertible, which is `Stacks.SymGraded.isInvertible_projectiveBundleTwist` at `n = 1`.

## Implementation notes

**Which twist datum.** Any twist datum of `Sym(ℰ)` carries a `ψ`, and Tag 01NR's uniqueness
assertion relates any two of them; the canonical one is used so that the map takes no datum as
an argument.

**Surjectivity is not asserted here.** The transpose of `ψ 1` is epimorphic exactly when the
twists are generated by the degree-one sections, and this file says nothing about that; see the
implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjRepresentsF1/TwistPowers.lean`, which measure what the
absolute shadow of that statement still needs. Both of the other clauses the splitting datum
wants of this map — that it lands on an invertible sheaf, and that its kernel is the
tautological subsheaf — are available: the first is proved below, the second is the categorical
kernel.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01OB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AYP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AYP)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists
open Stacks.SymGraded

universe u

namespace Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (E : X.Modules) (hqc : IsQuasicoherentPieces E)

/-- **The transpose of the homogeneous-section map of the canonical twist datum**: the map
`π^*Sym^n(ℰ) ⟶ 𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(n)` obtained from `ψ n` by the adjunction `π^* ⊣ π_*`. -/
def tautologicalTwistMap (n : ℕ) :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback (relativeProj (schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc)).toBase).obj
        ((schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc).piece (n : ℤ)) ⟶
      (projectiveBundleTwistData E hqc).algebra.piece (n : ℤ) :=
  ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction
    (relativeProj (schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc)).toBase).homEquiv _ _).symm
      ((projectiveBundleTwistData E hqc).ψ n)

/-- **The degree-one twist `𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(1)` as a module on the bundle.** The graded algebra of a
twist datum is indexed by the ringed site of the relative `Proj`; this names its degree-one
piece in the scheme's own category of modules, which is the category
`Stacks.Divisors.BundleSplittingDatum` states its fields in. -/
def tautologicalTwist : (relativeProj (schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc)).scheme.Modules :=
  (projectiveBundleTwistData E hqc).algebra.piece 1

/-- **The tautological map `π^*ℰ ⟶ 𝒪_{𝐏(ℰ)}(1)`**: the canonical map `ℰ ⟶ Sym¹(ℰ)` pulled back
to the bundle, followed by the transpose of the degree-one homogeneous-section map. -/
def tautologicalMap :
    (Scheme.Modules.pullback (relativeProj (schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc)).toBase).obj E ⟶
      tautologicalTwist E hqc :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pullback (relativeProj (schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc)).toBase).map
      (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen X E) ≫ tautologicalTwistMap E hqc 1

/-- **The target of the tautological map is invertible.** This is
`Stacks.SymGraded.isInvertible_projectiveBundleTwist` in degree one. -/
theorem isInvertible_tautologicalTwist [E.IsQuasicoherent] :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible
      (relativeProj (schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc)).scheme.presheaf
      (relativeProj (schemeSheafGradedAlgebra E hqc)).scheme.ringCatSheaf.2
      (tautologicalTwist E hqc) :=
  isInvertible_projectiveBundleTwist E hqc 1

end Stacks.ProjectiveBundleSplitting

end
